  DUT     : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 @ 115200, S/N A2WQS700B
  far end : swi_b (AT-x960-28YSQ) console u3 @ 9600, S/N A10737A261700021.  It runs a
            different build train from the DUT, so a working session cannot be an artefact
            of two identical images.
  link    : swi_d port1.0.2 <-> swi_b port1.0.2  (copper, trunk, vlan 60 tagged).  Rapid
            Spanning Tree leaves this the one FORWARDING link between the two switches.
  user    : the DUT logs in to swi_b as `cktmp`, a privilege 1 account.  swi_b carries
            `ssh server allow-users manager`, so that account is also named there.  Only
