  => STEP 2 PASS: the `port` argument is really used, because the refusal was specific to
     port 2222 at the same moment that port 22 on the same host was accepting.  The DUT is
     an SSH client and not only a TCP client, because it sends the SSH version string first.
     A client that sent nothing, a client whose packet was lost, and a client that reached a
     closed port are three different pictures here, and the capture holds two of them side
     by side.

